# ===========================================================================
# Stopping power exception list.  The first non-comment in this file must
# begin with the word EXCEPTION.  This causes RUMP to recognizes the file
# as a list of stopping power exception rules instead of a normal file.
#
# Each line is of the form:
#    z1  m1  z2   expr
#
#    z1   - incident particle Z
#    m1   - incident particle mass (closest INTEGER)
#    z2   - target particle Z (or pseudo Z)
#    expr - An analytical expression valid for all energies giving the
#           stopping power as a function of the energy (depicted as kev)
#           or of the Ziegler determined stopping power (zgl)
#
# Examples:
#  Scales Si values by 20 percent at all energies
#    2 4 14 zgl*1.2
#  Above 5 MeV, increase linearly by 1%/kev
#    2 4 14 (kev.lt.5000)?zgl:zgl*(1+.01*(kev-5000))
#  Use polynomial for mylar (z=93 in atom5.dat)
#    1 1 93 13.37-1.969E-2*kev+1.551E-5*kev^2-6.592E-9*kev^3+1.426E-12*kev^4-1.229E-16*kev^5
#    1 2 93 10.37-4.430E-4*kev-6.729E-6*kev^2+4.674E-9*kev^3-1.239E-12*kev^4+1.172E-16*kev^5
#    2 4 93 12.71+5.538E-2*kev-5.557E-5*kev^2+2.440E-8*kev^3-5.175E-12*kev^4+4.274E-16*kev^5
#
# Lines may be up to 256 characters in length and can be logically continued
# on the next line by ending with a \ character
# ===========================================================================

EXCEPTION TABLE

# Values for Mylar (used in stopping foils)
 1 1 93 13.37-1.969E-2*kev+1.551E-5*kev^2-6.592E-9*kev^3+1.426E-12*kev^4-1.229E-16*kev^5
 1 2 93 10.37-4.430E-4*kev-6.729E-6*kev^2+4.674E-9*kev^3-1.239E-12*kev^4+1.172E-16*kev^5
 2 4 93 12.71+5.538E-2*kev-5.557E-5*kev^2+2.440E-8*kev^3-5.175E-12*kev^4+4.274E-16*kev^5
